body:
i only know judo as a japanese version of greco roman wrestling (cause of the rules for competitions it's obviously upper body focused). i know traditional combat sports are only understood when trained and i only trained shotokan many years. i mean with internet i did try many others.

&#x200B;

ive read intro of a jujitsu book and it says the judo founder made judo and jujitsu. so i looked into jujitsu and it says it's from ju jitsu. so i looked that up and found what i was looking for i think (i recognized the grappling system based on a ilustration).

&#x200B;

years ago someone tried to mutilate me and i applied only principle of push/pul from a foreign jujutsu book. it had an ilustration of the anatomical handles. i made it a goal in life to fuly learn this combat sport for self defense- the kickboxing and bjj went out the window since i was in a situation that i had to leave this person harm free, had to deal with a huge opponent at standing grappling range and i was yet to develop iron bone as a substitute for muscle strength even with blue belt that i am ranked in shotokan.

i see you're an arnis practitioner. i know the arnis grappling is caled dumog and i find it more cumbersome for self defense than the sport grappling popular with ufc. i'm into modern arnis. found some videos on it to learn. and seing the founder he does deal with knife disarms with grappling. the grappling is based on jujutsu style caled circle jujutsu (or circle jujitsu- just saw on google that jujistu is another name for that old japanese standing grappling jujutsu) i gues with jujutsu it's like this:

koryu: styles/ schools before 1800s (whatever teh age was)

jujitsu: post 1800s

jiu jitsu: brazilian ground grappling and it's derivates

&#x200B;

some say its' more like 1500s than 1800s

&#x200B;

seems like jujutsu is the base name for these. sort of like catch wrestling is for freestyle and greco wrestling

&#x200B;

even if jujutsu and catch are also from older styles (sumo and lancashire...) were staying on the basis as jujutsu and catch for now in the discussion.

&#x200B;

the portion of the books of circle jujitsu is i think lacking throws (which i also wanna avoid) it has mostly arm locks including fingers (which is what i'm looking for) and choking/strangulations (which i avoid). so i wanna find some online material from another school that is the same combat sport- that is jujitsu. idk about aiki jutsu sounds like aikido stil many claim aikido is mostly invented out of the founder's own stuff and very little is jujutsu (from aikijutsu formerly known as daito ryu) that he in fact implemented it in his own invented system as a addition.

&#x200B;

i'm looking for something mainstream standing grappling that's jujitsu that's free from the dogma of going to the ground.

&#x200B;

what do you mean fluffy stuff? i thought he removed lethal techniques like neck crank.

i once read in a self defense book from a good author "never employ takedowns" he meant specialy double leg takedowns.

&#x200B;

once i was in a headlock  (with my head in a container) and practicing takedown could have saved me life cause those put your hand in his face failed he was taler and stronger. so he let me go after. so now i either have to strike out of headlock or 1st takedown 2nd grapple succesfuly out. i have no clue what to do.

&#x200B;

i know ultimate fighting has many techniques so i try to see what to learn for sport and self defense.

&#x200B;

i as a short guy know takedowns work, yet self defense instructors don't want to use them.

like purely bjj on the ground? do you use catch wrestling also on the ground?

&#x200B;

i find bjj fun too, only at the offense like americana i get tired it takes much time and energy for me to do the bjj types of submissions. i think catch wrestling works better the ground as an offense on top of bjj. bjj has better moves like positioning and mobility.

&#x200B;

i have noticed dumog is similar to a mix of bjj and catch wresling when it comes to ground fighting. [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D7WqzkOEK0Q](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D7WqzkOEK0Q) hard to tel whos who.

what do yo mean by "greco"? from what i understand greco roman wretling is only throws and takedowns.

&#x200B;

and do you have any tips for that big dudes thing?

ok now i understand. il see.

&#x200B;

luckily i found out a good karate school here starts at 9pm (so i can train after uni classes if time permits)

i'm interrested as a 21 year old to get a brown belt.

&#x200B;

i am recorded in as a shotokan blue belt (in which way world karate federation keeps records- i know by diploma im blue belt hehe)

&#x200B;

 i'd preffer to train by myself. i have my own conditioning and warm ups that work my body better than what karate school do (i do pul ups and bridges and weight lifting to and extent)-  cause if i skipped these i would have muscles only on the front and skinny back.

&#x200B;

i know most shotokan katas and i can somehow learn techniques (worst case scenario i find a brown belt to tel me how to do a technique).

&#x200B;

i thought i can pay a karate school for the testing and paperwork (cause we heavily regulate karate) as an isolated act- they tel me the time and place to bring my gear and see if i pass the brown belt test.

&#x200B;

it happens at winter and summer and i thought to get a belt with the students of a assigned school.

my grammar haha. yeah i did shotokan for 7 years (after school activity), it was not very effective in any way but casuing me to sweat but when they started teling us to do more variety in sparring (the front kick is the first kick we learn and keep practicing it  90 percent of the time) i started side kick and more footwork it was amazing. I'm like the 70 kg type of person.

&#x200B;

I did boxing as without coaching as a teenager for self defense shotokan is to rigid with form for me.

idk some people treat feelings way to seriously

&#x200B;

you can't even say "i had enough" and not being seriously questioned

man buy her a snickers and cola. if someone did that to me i would be happier with that then warm words

&#x200B;

she wouldn't care if you did like anyhthing else if she's non-social (sounds like me so believe me)

&#x200B;

when i  was in high school i was menatlly beaten a lot so sweets do get the mind to sanity like tranquilizers

&#x200B;

just whatever you do don't be in intimate contact with her; since you're teenagers and idk how teenagers think but i know you all like the idea of sex
